#====================================================================
# E140 — OpenHarmony toolchains use OHOS or HarmonyOS as CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME
#====================================================================

id:                     E267
trigger_tool:           cmake
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=OHOS|CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=HarmonyOS|CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME:STRING=OHOS|CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME:STRING=HarmonyOS|System is unknown to cmake|OS_LINUX not defined

severity:               2
category:               platform-cmake-detection
match_keywords:         CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, OHOS, HarmonyOS, OS_LINUX, platform detection, target_compile_definitions, object library

root_cause:             OpenHarmony toolchains do not use CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux consistently: the official SDK uses OHOS while the adapted Conan toolchain may use HarmonyOS, so Linux-only or single-spelling platform guards silently miss one build path
affected_scope:         CMake projects and reusable modules that route Unix behavior, shared-library metadata, feature checks, or platform macros by CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME
verification_cmd:       grep -R -E 'CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME.*(OHOS|HarmonyOS)' CMakeLists.txt cmake 2>/dev/null

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           add-harmonyos-cmake-detection
rec_description:        Match both official spellings with CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^(OHOS|HarmonyOS)$" for OpenHarmony-specific routing; when source behavior depends on that decision, inject a project-local PRIVATE feature macro into the target that actually compiles the source, including the underlying object-library target created by build helpers
rec_command:            grep -R -E 'CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME.*(OHOS|HarmonyOS)|target_compile_definitions' CMakeLists.txt cmake 2>/dev/null
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual-edit

forbid_1_pattern:       CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME (STREQUAL|MATCHES) "?(OHOS|HarmonyOS)"?
forbid_1_reason:        Matching only one spelling makes local official-SDK validation and Conan CI take different platform branches
forbid_1_consequence:   Platform flags, target properties, dependency routing, or shared-library behavior can differ between local validation and CI without a configure error

causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             [E007, E159]
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               doc/E267.md
last_updated:           2026-07-20
source_event:           rocksdb 6.4.6 compile; Cling 1.3 official SDK and Conan target-graph comparison; PR #2936 compile-database verification of obj.clingInterpreter


